# Smart Search & Location Enrichment Engine

This document outlines the plan for fixing the "0 buses found" search issue and building a robust search mechanism that relies on physical location and real-time graph routing, bypassing the limitations of the Margdarshi API's missing route metadata.

## Goal Description

Currently, searching for a specific city or region (like "Saharanpur") yields no active buses because the external API rarely provides route names or next stops. To resolve this, we will pass the real-time physical location (`zone_name`) to the frontend search engine. In the future phases, we will build predictive AI route assignments and a Smart Journey Search using our graph engine.

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Immediate Search Fix (Zone Name Integration)

We will inject `zone_name` from the Margdarshi Live Tracking API down to the frontend UI, allowing users to search buses based on their physical location strings (e.g. "Meerut", "Saharanpur").

